cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Prompt-CAM: Making Vision Transformers Interpretable for Fine-Grained Analysis"
message: >-
  If you find this software helpful in your research, please
  cite both the software and our paper (see README for the
  paper citation).
type: software
authors:
- given-names: Arpita
  family-names: Chowdhury
  affiliation: The Ohio State University
- given-names: Elizabeth G.
  family-names: Campolongo
  affiliation: The Ohio State University
abstract: >-
  We present a simple usage of pre-trained Vision
  Transformers (ViTs) for fine-grained analysis, aiming to
  identify and localize the traits that distinguish visually
  similar categories, such as different bird species or dog
  breeds.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Imageomics/Prompt_CAM'
keywords:
  - explainable-ai
  - interpretable-ai
  - imageomics
  - fine-grained-classification
  - vision-transformer
  - interpretable
license: MIT
